@startuml seq_dia_read_dids
title SC-DIA-02 - Read identification DIDs in the application, PBL and SBL

participant "UDS tester" as Tester
box "TCU"
participant "Application" as App
participant "PBL" as PBL
participant "SBL" as SBL
end box

note over Tester, SBL
Covers: SYS-DIA-005, SYS-DIA-001, SYS-DIA-002, SIM-TST-003
UDS requests on DIAG_PhysReq 0x7E1, responses on DIAG_Resp 0x7E9 (can_matrix section 5).
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
The TCU is split into its software parts because the DIDs depend on the running part (reprogramming section 4).
end note

group application running (default or extended session)
  Tester -> App : 22 F1 80
  App --> Tester : 62 F1 80 <major> <minor> <patch> 00
  note right: PBL software version
  Tester -> App : 22 F1 81
  App --> Tester : 62 F1 81 <sw_version, 4 bytes>
  note right: application version from the image header
  Tester -> App : 22 F1 86
  App --> Tester : 62 F1 86 01 (default) or 03 (extended)
  Tester -> App : 22 F1 87
  App --> Tester : 62 F1 87 <ASCII xAT-TCU padded with spaces, 16 bytes>
  Tester -> App : 22 F1 8C
  App --> Tester : 62 F1 8C <MCU unique ID, 16 bytes>
  Tester -> App : 22 F1 5A
  App --> Tester : 62 F1 5A <tester id (2), date YYMMDD BCD (3), reserved (11)>
  Tester -> App : 22 FD 00
  App --> Tester : 62 FD 00 <programming counter, 2 bytes>
  Tester -> App : 22 FD 01
  App --> Tester : 7F 22 31
  note right: requestOutOfRange (ISO 14229-1):\nFD01 exists only in the SBL
end

group PBL running (default or programming session)
  Tester -> PBL : 22 F1 80, F1 87, F1 8C, F1 5A, FD 00
  PBL --> Tester : 62 ... as in the application
  Tester -> PBL : 22 F1 81
  PBL --> Tester : 62 F1 81 <sw_version> or 62 F1 81 FF FF FF FF
  note right: 0xFFFFFFFF if the application is invalid
  Tester -> PBL : 22 F1 86
  PBL --> Tester : 62 F1 86 01 (default) or 02 (programming)
  Tester -> PBL : 22 FD 01
  PBL --> Tester : 7F 22 31
  note right: requestOutOfRange (ISO 14229-1)
end

group SBL running (programming session)
  Tester -> SBL : 22 F1 80, F1 81, F1 87, F1 8C, F1 5A, FD 00
  SBL --> Tester : 62 ... as in the PBL
  Tester -> SBL : 22 F1 86
  SBL --> Tester : 62 F1 86 02
  Tester -> SBL : 22 FD 01
  SBL --> Tester : 62 FD 01 <SBL software version, 4 bytes>
end

note over Tester, SBL: F15A and FD00 come from the newest valid boot info record (reprogramming section 7); the SBL writes F15A at step 12 (SC-BOOT-01).
@enduml
